      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs: propose durable session task runtime RFC v2",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw has strong sessions, Gateway, tasks, subagents, and operator surfaces, but long-running multi-agent work still needs a small core contract for durable session/task runtime state: run identity, step identity, event ordering, child links, recovery markers, and read-only inspection.\n\nThis PR is the RFC/architecture decision point for that boundary. It replaces the older RFC discussion in #97507 with updated naming and scope:\n\n- `durable_runtime_*` instead of workflow-oriented schema naming;\n- runtime runs/steps/events/refs/signals/timers/links as the core primitives;\n- local-first shared state DB posture;\n- Task Flow, Workboard, Work module, and external PM tools as projections/follow-ups, not prerequisites;\n- no product-specific terminology.\n\n## Dependency Chain\n\nThis is PR1 in the replacement durable runtime stack:\n\n1. PR1: RFC v2 docs only, this PR.\n2. PR2: durable runtime foundation, schema/store/CLI/Gateway read-only inspection.\n3. PR3: agent/session/subagent wiring on top of PR2.\n\nPR2 and PR3 should be reviewed only after this boundary is acceptable.\n\n## Scope\n\nDocs only. No runtime behavior changes.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAuthored evidence for the docs-only RFC:\n\n- `node scripts/generate-docs-map.mjs --check` passed after regenerating `docs/docs_map.md`.\n- `node scripts/docs-list.js` lists `specs/durable-session-task-runtime-rfc.md`.\n- `git diff --check` passed locally before push.\n- Runtime proof is intentionally not applicable: this PR only adds the RFC document and generated docs map entry. The behavior proof for disabled/enabled durable runtime paths is attached to PR2.\n\n## Notes\n\nThe older PRs #97507 and #97508 are intentionally left open while reviewers inspect this replacement stack. They can be closed after the new stack has review feedback.\n",
